add('A small garden plan','DAN, MAYA, NINA','HOME_KITCHEN','Medium three-shot across the familiar oak island.','Maya opens a garden notebook beside two nursery seedlings. Nina puts a closed radish packet beside it; Dan makes room for the plan. Add title editorially inside this shot.','Later spring morning after Ruth’s visit; island clean; one mint and one basil nursery seedling, closed radish packet; no soil indoors.','Open notebook and closed packet on island; both seedlings still in their original nursery pots.','Same W01 wardrobe and kitchen; no harvested food or new plant growth.','MAYA|A small garden today. Mint, basil, and a few radishes.','DAN|Small garden. Ambitious gardener.','NINA|Then let us give the gardener a plan.')
add('A word with two jobs','MAX, DAN, ELLA','HOME_KITCHEN','Child-height medium view of Max and a scrap of paper.','Max hears mint and draws one pretend coin on a scrap of paper. Ella watches while Dan leans close to understand the drawing.','Two live seedlings remain on island; Max has one blank scrap and a pencil; no real coins present.','One paper coin drawing lies beside the notebook; no soil or plant has been touched.','The drawing is pretend paper, never currency or a seed.','MAX|Mint? Are we growing money?','DAN|That would be a very useful garden.','ELLA|Our shopping list might get smaller.')
add('Leaves instead of change','MAYA, MAX, DAN','HOME_KITCHEN','Close three-shot with the mint seedling between faces.','Maya points to the mint plant’s leaves without picking one. Max compares the plant with his paper coin, then smiles at the two meanings.','Mint seedling untouched in nursery pot; pretend coin drawing flat beside notebook.','Max understands mint is a plant here; coin drawing remains dry on the island.','No coin enters a pot; no claim money can grow.','MAYA|This mint is an herb. The other mint makes coins.','MAX|Two jobs, one word.','DAN|And only one belongs in our garden.')
add('Three homes for plants','NINA, LEO, ELLA','HOME_KITCHEN','Over Nina’s shoulder onto the open notebook; text added as SVG.','Nina sketches three positions. Leo assigns mint left, basil center and radish seeds right; Ella points to each empty circle in turn.','Notebook open; no garden pots delivered; two seedlings and closed seed packet on island.','Plan has three ordered positions; all plants and packet remain untransferred.','Positions are viewed from the path facing the fence: mint LEFT, basil CENTER, radish RIGHT.','NINA|Mint left, basil in the middle, radishes on the right.','LEO|Three pots. Three saucers.','ELLA|And three labels that tell the truth.')
add('A delivery we can count','DAN, LEO, MAYA','HOME_KITCHEN','Medium Dan beside Leo’s notebook.','Leo checks a note saying Ben will bring three empty pots. Dan checks the clear route to the garden; Maya carries the notebook away from the seedlings.','Ben not yet arrived; no terracotta pots indoors; garden path clear.','Maya holds notebook; Dan and Leo ready to receive three empty pots outside.','Ben is Dan’s brother and a brief supporting visitor; not a seventh family member.','DAN|My brother Ben is bringing the pots.','LEO|Empty ones?','MAYA|Yes. We are supplying the plants, not ordering a forest.')
add('Tools have places too','NINA, ELLA, MAX','HOME_KITCHEN','Medium near the garden doorway, clean supply tray in foreground.','Nina puts six pairs of gardening gloves, three blank label stakes and a pencil into a clean tray. Ella keeps the unopened seed packet upright beside them.','Supplies clean on island; seed packet closed; seedlings remain in their nursery pots.','Tray holds gloves, three blank stakes, pencil and closed seed packet; no loose soil inside.','Garden tools and soil will remain outdoors; no food utensils borrowed.','ELLA|Labels and gloves are ready.','MAX|Do the seeds need tiny gloves?','NINA|No. Just our careful hands.')
add('A drink with a different job','DAN, MAYA, MAX','HOME_KITCHEN','Medium two-shot with Max at frame edge; a green watering can by the door.','Dan lifts the empty green watering can from the doorway. Maya reminds him that garden water belongs in garden tools, while Max leaves drinking glasses inside.','One empty green watering can by door; no measured water in it yet.','Dan holds the empty can; all kitchen cups and glasses stay indoors.','The later 100 mL garden measure is a dedicated marked garden cup, never a drinking cup.','DAN|I will bring their drink.','MAYA|Bring the can first. We will check the soil outside.','MAX|No straws for the basil, then.')
add('Outside together','DAN, MAYA, NINA, LEO, ELLA, MAX','GARDEN_PATH','Wide doorway-to-path move, house left and tree right.','All six go outside together. Nina carries the two nursery seedlings in one shallow crate; Ella carries the supply tray, Maya the notebook with the dry paper drawing tucked inside its cover, and Dan the empty can.','No terracotta pots yet; seedlings in crate; tray packed; clear paved route to bench.','All six stand near the sunny bench; supplies set on its right end; no potting started.','Carry supplies without blocking the path; nursery seedlings are existing plants, not newly germinated seeds.','NINA|Stay on the clear path with your hands free of soil.','DAN|Even my grand plan is walking carefully.','LEO|That is a good first step.')
add('Uncle Ben brings empty homes','BEN, DAN, MAYA','GARDEN_PATH','Medium at the garden gate; Ben faces Dan without obscuring the path.','Ben arrives carrying one stack of three empty terracotta pots and a separate tied stack of three matching saucers. Dan accepts the pot stack with both hands.','Ben entering gate; Dan empty-handed after setting the empty can by bench; no terracotta pots yet on bench.','Dan holds three nested empty pots; Ben still holds three saucers; Maya stands clear.','BEN cameo begins; provisional olive overshirt/cream tee/brown trousers/beard design. Three pots only.','BEN|Three empty homes, as promised.','DAN|Excellent. Their new residents are already waiting.','MAYA|Hello, Ben. Thank you for bringing them.')
add('No hidden forest','BEN, NINA, LEO','GARDEN_PATH','Medium saucer handoff; empty pot rims visible on bench behind.','After Dan sets the nested pots on the bench, Ben passes three saucers to Nina. Leo counts the three rims without unstacking anything himself.','Three nested pots now on bench; Ben holds three tied saucers; Nina ready to receive.','Nina holds all three saucers; Ben’s hands empty; three pots remain on bench.','All delivered vessels are EMPTY; no seedling or coin concealed in the stack.','LEO|Three pots and three saucers. Nothing growing yet.','BEN|Not even a surprise tree.','NINA|That keeps our small plan small.')
add('The family resemblance','BEN, DAN, MAX, MAYA','GARDEN_PATH','Warm medium three-shot by the gate, bench kept on the same screen side.','Maya hands Max the dry paper coin drawing from the notebook cover. Max holds it and tells Ben the joke. Dan laughs with his brother; no one takes a coin toward soil.','Delivered pots and saucers on bench; Maya holds the dry notebook with the paper drawing inside; Max’s hands empty; no planting.','Ben has seen the paper drawing; Max keeps it above waist height and away from the work surface.','A joke about mint never becomes a magical money plant; Ben does not solve the planting task.','MAX|We nearly ordered a money plant.','BEN|Dan once labeled an empty box “treasure.”','DAN|It contained very valuable possibilities.')
add('A short visit, a real thank-you','BEN, DAN, MAYA, MAX','GARDEN_PATH','Medium farewell at open gate; family remains inside.','Max returns the drawing to Maya’s notebook. Ben waves and leaves through the gate; Dan closes it. Maya carries the notebook and drawing back to the bench.','Ben by gate with empty hands; pots and saucers delivered; no new plants.','Ben off-screen and departed; gate shut; original six remain in garden.','Final BEN shot: four 15-second slots, 60 seconds total. No later Ben voice, hand or face.','BEN|Enjoy your garden. Label first, guess later.','DAN|A useful family motto. Thanks, Ben.','MAYA|We will show you the journal next time.')
add('Look under the pot','MAYA, ELLA, DAN','POTTING_BENCH','Close low angle on an adult-held empty pot; faces above the rim.','Maya un-nests the pots one at a time and shows Ella a drainage hole without putting a finger through it. Dan sets each pot upright on the bench.','Three empty nested pots and three saucers on bench; gloves still in tray.','Three separate empty pots stand left, center and right; three saucers stacked aside.','Adults lift heavy terracotta; no pot is broken or dropped.','ELLA|There is a hole in the bottom.','MAYA|Extra water needs a way out.','DAN|A pot with an exit. Sensible architecture.')
add('The water has a starting line','NINA, LEO, DAN','GARDEN_PATH','Medium at the outdoor tap; marked garden jug and green can visible.','Nina measures 500 mL at the outdoor tap in a dedicated marked garden jug and pours it into the empty green can. Leo records the starting amount; tap closes.','Green can empty; garden jug empty; no soil prepared; children stand back from tap.','Can contains exactly 500 mL water; jug empty; tap OFF; Leo notes 500 mL starting water.','Numbers supplied by WATER_RECORD.svg; no additional water is drawn during this episode.','LEO|Five hundred milliliters in the can.','DAN|That sounds satisfyingly official.','NINA|It is a record, not an instruction to use it all.')
add('Seedlings are already plants','NINA, MAYA, MAX','POTTING_BENCH','Medium down the bench; two nursery plants framed separately.','Nina lifts mint and basil from their carrying crate and sets their nursery pots near the matching left and center positions. Maya leaves the radish packet closed at right.','Three empty terracotta pots separate; two seedlings still in crate; closed seed packet in tray.','Mint nursery pot beside left terracotta pot; basil beside center; closed radish packet beside right; crate empty.','Seedling foliage exists before planting; radish pot must stay bare until a later real day.','MAX|Those two already have leaves.','MAYA|They are young plants. The radishes start as seeds.','NINA|Different beginnings, the same careful attention.')
add('A workbench, not a playground','DAN, ELLA, LEO','POTTING_BENCH','Medium with clear hand space around three pots.','Dan sets one small blunt garden trowel and one dedicated 100 mL garden measure on the bench. Ella moves the tray away from the edge; Leo checks the path.','Three terracotta pots empty; water can with 500 mL on ground safely beside bench; tool tray closed.','Blunt trowel and empty marked measure on bench; tray stable; path clear.','No sharp shovel, kitchen spoon, climbing on bench or tool swinging.','DAN|Tools here. Clear path there.','ELLA|And nobody swings the shovel.','LEO|Especially our ambitious gardener.')
add('Saucers under empty pots','MAYA, NINA, ELLA','POTTING_BENCH','Bench-height three-shot; all three pot positions visible.','Maya and Nina place one saucer under each pot. Ella names the fixed left-to-right order without moving the pots herself.','Three empty pots upright; three saucers stacked aside; two nursery seedlings nearby.','Three empty terracotta pots each on one saucer in left-center-right order.','Saucers catch drainage, not permanent pools; their final empty state will be shown.','ELLA|Left for mint, middle for basil, right for radishes.','NINA|Each pot gets its own saucer.','MAYA|Now the bench has a clear plan.')
add('The pretend coin gets a job','MAX, LEO, DAN','POTTING_BENCH','Close notebook insert, then Max’s pleased reaction.','Leo clips Max’s dry paper coin drawing to the OUTSIDE of the notebook cover as a joke reminder. Dan points from that drawing to the mint nursery plant.','Paper drawing in notebook cover; notebook dry; no labels written yet; all pots empty.','Drawing clipped to notebook cover, away from soil; all three blank stakes still in tray.','Paper coin is never buried, watered, used as fertilizer or exchanged as real money.','MAX|Can my coin help?','LEO|It can remind us which mint we mean.','DAN|A very profitable piece of paper.')
add('Six gardeners, one safe plan','DAN, MAYA, NINA, LEO, ELLA, MAX','POTTING_BENCH','Wide six-person bench setup; no seventh actor.','All six put on their own gardening gloves. Maya keeps the seedlings to one side; Nina positions the closed soil bag low on the bench before opening it herself.','Pots empty; gloves in tray; closed soil bag below bench; Ben gone.','All six gloved; Nina holds closed soil bag low; paper drawing remains on notebook cover.','Hands kept away from mouths; no dust play, tasting, fertilizer or pesticide.','NINA|Gloves on, hands away from mouths.','MAYA|We will wash properly when we finish.','DAN|The plants are not the only things getting good care.')
add('Open gently','NINA, MAYA, LEO','POTTING_BENCH','Medium adult hands at the low-opened soil bag, Leo beyond arm’s reach.','Nina opens the bag of already slightly damp potting mix close to the bench. Maya steadies it; Leo waits with the empty blunt trowel until the adults invite him.','Closed damp mix bag low on bench; pots empty; all six gloved; water untouched at 500 mL.','Soil bag open without visible dust cloud; trowel rests on tray; no pot filled yet.','Damp potting mix is not food; adult opens and handles bag, no airborne dust.','LEO|It is already a little damp.','NINA|Yes. We will check before adding water.','MAYA|Slowly keeps the soil where it belongs.')
add('Room for roots','MAYA, DAN, ELLA','POTTING_BENCH','Medium over the three pot rims from the path-facing side.','Maya and Dan fill the three pots with damp mix, leaving space for the two root balls and a lower watering rim. Ella watches the three levels. Use an explicit work-time dissolve.','Three empty pots on saucers; two nursery seedlings and closed seed packet aside; mix bag open.','Three pots contain damp mix; left and center have root-ball hollows, right has a level seed bed; no plant transferred.','One work ellipsis, no instant soil teleport; no fourth pot.','ELLA|Leave room at the top?','MAYA|Yes. Room for water without spilling soil.','DAN|Even a pot appreciates a little breathing space.')
add('Check before the pour','NINA, DAN, MAX','POTTING_BENCH','Close adult finger checking mix at the right pot’s rim.','Nina tests the dampness of the mix with a gloved fingertip. Dan lifts the still-closed green can as if to make a generous pour, then pauses when she gestures to check first.','Pots contain damp mix; can still holds all 500 mL; no water added.','Dan sets can down without pouring; soil remains damp; all 500 mL retained.','The oversized watering idea is stopped before overwatering or plant harm.','DAN|One generous drink for everyone?','NINA|Check first. Damp soil does not need a flood.','MAX|Let us not give the roots a swimming pool.')
add('Look, do not taste','MAYA, MAX, ELLA','POTTING_BENCH','Child-height medium; Maya holds the mint nursery pot securely.','Max leans to look at the mint leaves without touching his mouth or picking a leaf. Maya keeps the plant steady and invites a careful visual comparison.','Mint still in nursery pot; basil still in nursery pot; three soil-filled terracotta pots unplanted.','Both seedlings intact; Max’s gloved hands rest below the bench edge; no leaf picked.','No tasting plants, soil or seeds; gardening and food preparation remain separate.','MAX|It looks much greener than money.','MAYA|Today we are planting, not tasting.','ELLA|Its leaves are the better clue anyway.')
add('Find the mint label','LEO, DAN, MAYA','POTTING_BENCH','Over Leo’s shoulder onto nursery tag; readable word added editorially.','Leo compares the nursery mint tag with the left circle in the notebook. Dan names the match; Maya positions the left pot for transplanting.','Mint and basil still in separate nursery pots; three damp soil beds ready.','Left terracotta pot is ready beneath Maya’s hands; mint identity verified; basil untouched.','Mint remains LEFT throughout bench and final ground arrangement; never swap labels to fit camera.','LEO|The tag says mint. Left pot.','DAN|I checked the label before guessing.','MAYA|A strong start for our ambitious gardener.')
add('A small root ball','MAYA, ELLA, DAN','POTTING_BENCH','Close Maya’s gloved hands supporting mint over the empty hollow.','Maya gently eases the mint root ball from its nursery pot, supporting the soil rather than pulling leaves. Dan holds the now-empty nursery pot aside.','Mint in its nursery container beside prepared left hollow; basil untouched at center.','Mint root ball supported in Maya’s hands over left hollow; empty mint nursery pot in Dan’s hand.','Only adults release root balls; do not turn mint into bare seeds or duplicate a plant.','ELLA|You are holding the roots, not tugging the leaves.','MAYA|Exactly. Gentle hands underneath.','DAN|No plant gets pulled by its hairstyle.')
add('Mint finds its home','MAYA, MAX, NINA','POTTING_BENCH','Bench-level medium on the left terracotta pot.','Maya lowers the single mint root ball into the left hollow at its original soil level. Nina adds a little mix around it while Max watches clear of the trowel.','Mint root ball above left hollow; left pot not yet planted; center and right soil-filled but bare.','One mint plant established in LEFT pot; center and right still bare; no water yet.','Same one mint plant, not a second seedling; can water remains 500 mL.','MAX|It has moved house.','NINA|Without changing its name.','MAYA|Now we support the roots with soil.')
add('Firm, not squashed','ELLA, MAYA, LEO','POTTING_BENCH','Close Ella’s supervised gloved fingertips around the mint soil edge.','With Maya guiding, Ella lightly firms only the soil around the mint root ball. Leo keeps the plant’s leaves clear of their gloves.','Mint in left pot with loose surrounding mix; basil nursery plant waiting; right bare.','Mint upright and soil gently settled; no crushed leaves, water or label yet.','No hard tamping; keep stem at original planting depth and foliage intact.','ELLA|Like tucking in a blanket?','MAYA|Gently. The roots still need air.','LEO|Comfortable, not squashed.')
add('An empty nursery container','DAN, NINA, MAX','POTTING_BENCH','Medium Dan setting the empty nursery pot in the carrying crate.','Dan checks that the mint nursery container is empty and places it in the crate for later cleaning and reuse. Nina keeps the basil nursery plant separate.','Mint planted left; one empty mint nursery container in Dan’s hand; crate empty.','Empty mint nursery container in crate; basil nursery container still holds its one plant.','Empty packaging is not a fourth garden pot or a duplicate mint.','DAN|One empty nursery pot, ready to use another day.','MAX|So the plant has not left a twin behind.','NINA|Only its old address.')
add('A different leaf','NINA, ELLA, LEO','POTTING_BENCH','Close basil leaves and nursery tag, both children behind the pot.','Nina turns the basil nursery pot so its own tag faces the family. Ella compares the broader leaves without plucking one; Leo checks the center circle.','Mint planted LEFT; basil still in nursery container; center hollow empty; radish bed bare.','Basil identity confirmed for CENTER; no plant moved yet.','Basil and mint are distinct existing seedlings; no edible sampling.','ELLA|The leaves look different.','NINA|This is basil. Its tag agrees.','LEO|Middle pot, just as we planned.')
add('Support the basil','NINA, DAN, MAX','POTTING_BENCH','Close adult hands above the center pot, Max in soft background.','Nina eases the basil root ball out while Dan takes the empty nursery container. Max points only after Nina’s hands have a secure hold.','Basil in nursery container beside center hollow; mint left; radish bed bare.','Basil root ball supported above center pot; its empty nursery container in Dan’s hand.','Adults handle root ball; no extra basil plant or leaf picking.','MAX|Another moving day.','NINA|And the same gentle lift.','DAN|Our garden has excellent movers.')
add('Basil in the middle','NINA, MAYA, ELLA','POTTING_BENCH','Medium on the center pot with mint visible at frame left.','Nina lowers the single basil root ball into the center hollow. Maya adds damp mix around it while Ella keeps the label stakes dry in the tray.','Mint LEFT established; basil root ball above CENTER; RIGHT seed bed bare; water 500 mL.','One basil plant established CENTER; mint LEFT; RIGHT bare; empty second nursery pot in crate after Dan sets it there.','One mint and one basil only; two empty nursery containers now in crate.','NINA|Basil in the middle.','MAYA|Soil around the roots, below the rim.','ELLA|I have its label ready for later.')
add('Leave the leaves room','LEO, NINA, DAN','POTTING_BENCH','Close supervised hands around basil soil; Dan framed at bench end.','Leo gently firms the basil’s surrounding soil with Nina’s guidance. Dan shifts the empty crate under the bench, away from the clear path.','Basil planted center with loose surrounding mix; two empty nursery containers in crate atop bench.','Basil upright and soil settled; crate with two empty nursery containers safely under bench.','Both leafy plants remain upright; radish bed still bare; no water used.','LEO|Not too tight around the stem.','NINA|That is right. Support it without squeezing.','DAN|A comfortable fit, even without shoe sizes.')
add('Two plants, two names','MAYA, MAX, ELLA','POTTING_BENCH','Medium view across left and center pots, right pot visible bare.','Maya asks Max what belongs where while he checks the notebook. Ella smiles as he names the mint and basil correctly without turning it into an audience exercise.','Mint LEFT and basil CENTER planted; RIGHT pot bare damp seed bed; stakes blank.','Max identifies both positions; all three pots remain stationary; no labels inserted yet.','The question serves the family’s planting task, no viewer repetition or quiz overlay.','MAYA|Which plant is in the middle?','MAX|Basil. The mint is not making change on the left.','ELLA|Good. Our garden names are staying put.')
